new('daigné','daigner','verb past participle','deigned; consented graciously',['refused','forgotten','hesitated'],'Le souverain a bien voulu répondre, malgré sa position supérieure : il a ___ me répondre.',['daigné','voulu','pu','dû'],'Quel participe signifie a bien voulu faire quelque chose, en marquant une faveur ou une supériorité ?',note='The giant credits the Creator with graciously consenting to reveal secrets. Daigner has no published or earlier family; the past participle and later conditional form share one lexical sense rather than separate tense meanings. All four participles fit il a followed immediately by me répondre; only daigné adds the explicitly described gracious or condescending consent.')
new('découvrir','découvrir','verb infinitive disclosure','reveal; make known to someone',['hide','withhold','disguise'],'Pour lui faire connaître ce secret encore caché, il veut le lui ___.',['découvrir','cacher','taire','dissimuler'],'Quel infinitif signifie révéler ou faire connaître à quelqu’un ce qui était caché ?','new:lem_parure_decouvrir_verb_85904ca65e',note='Me découvrir des secrets makes information known to the giant. The global family’s uncover-material and find/learn-for-oneself senses do not express this recipient-directed disclosure. Académie 1762 révéler gives découvrir as disclose unknown secret knowledge. Prepare that meaning on the existing découvrir lemma and preserve discovery mastery.')
new('semblaient','sembler','verb imperfect plural','seemed; appeared to be',['became','remained','disappeared'],'Sans savoir s’ils l’étaient vraiment, on avait l’impression qu’ils étaient impossibles à comprendre : ces secrets ___ impénétrables.',['semblaient','devenaient','restaient','disparaissaient'],'Quel verbe à l’imparfait pluriel indique une apparence plutôt qu’un état assuré ?','sns_parure_sembler_paraitre_avoir_une_certaine_qualite_ou_une_certaine_maniere_d_etre_avoir_l_air_l_apparence_8cfb5497c5',note='The secrets had appeared inaccessible before the revelation. Global sembler senses were read; the explicit appearance definition covers the source. Only semblaient qualifies a perceived impression; devenir/rester assert change or continuation, and disparaître does not assert appearance.')
new('impénétrables','impénétrable','adjective plural figurative','unfathomable; impossible to understand',['clear','explainable','obvious'],'Ces secrets ne peuvent être compris ni sondés par l’esprit : ils paraissent ___.',['impénétrables','clairs','explicables','évidents'],'Quel adjectif pluriel décrit des mystères que l’intelligence ne parvient pas à sonder ?',note='The secrets’ inaccessibility is intellectual, not a physically impermeable wall or forest. No published or earlier impénétrable family exists. All alternatives are plural adjective predicates; inability to understand, not spelling agreement, selects the target.')
new('daignerait','daigner','verb conditional singular','would deign; would consent graciously',['would refuse','would forget','would hesitate'],'Si le souverain nous accordait cette faveur, il ___ nous recevoir.',['daignerait','voudrait','pourrait','devrait'],'Quel verbe au conditionnel signifie voudrait bien accorder cette faveur ?','prior-bank:chapter-06-batch-03.json:daigné_chapter_06_03_150_137',note='Ne daignerait-on pas vous regarder concerns whether courtiers would condescend to notice the tiny humans. It shares daigné’s gracious/condescending consent meaning and the same planned lemma/sense; conditional inflection alone creates no sense. The target is the already authored bank in this exact package.')

new('offre','offrir','verb present first singular','offer; present for acceptance',['refuse','withdraw','forget'],'Je propose mon aide pour que vous puissiez l’accepter : je vous l’___.',['offre','refuse','retire','oublie'],'Quel verbe après je vous l’ signifie propose quelque chose à votre acceptation ?','sns_parure_offrir_presenter_quelque_chose_a_quelqu_un_en_souhaitant_qu_il_l_accepte_d03d71a1cf',note='The giant offers protection to the humans. The published offrir definition explicitly covers presenting something for acceptance and is not limited to physical objects. Its reflexive treat-oneself sense is excluded; this first-person surface shares the offer sense.')
new('protection','protection','noun feminine singular','protection; support against harm',['punishment','threat','abandonment'],'L’aide promise pour les défendre contre un danger est une ___.',['protection','punition','menace','désertion'],'Quel nom féminin désigne une aide qui met à l’abri d’un danger ?',note='The giant promises to safeguard the people. No published or earlier protection family exists. Protection/punition/menace/désertion are feminine singular and fit une; only support shielding someone from harm satisfies the middle clue.')
new('jamais','jamais','adverb positive comparative','ever; at any time',['never','already','soon'],'Il le comprend aujourd’hui plus fortement qu’à aucun autre moment : il le comprend plus que ___.',['jamais','souvent','déjà','bientôt'],'Quel adverbe, après plus que, compare le présent à tout moment antérieur ?','prior:chapter-05-identity-plan.json:jamais_chapter_05_held_01_124',occ=[(163,59)],note='Plus que jamais means more than ever, without negating the action. The earlier positive-ever planned sense already contrasts any possible occasion with negative never; this comparative context uses that same any-time value. Extend its bank to the comparative construction rather than create a third jamais sense or reuse the published never-only questions.')
new('eu','avoir','past participle existential','been; existed in there has been',['owned','lost','received'],'Pour parler de l’existence passée d’une personne étonnée, on dit : il y a ___ quelqu’un d’étonné.',['eu','perdu','reçu','gardé'],'Quel participe complète il y a pour dire qu’une personne a existé ou a été présente ?','sns_fr_avoir_existential',note='In il y a eu quelqu’un, a is the outer compound auxiliary and eu is the participle of existential avoir. The legacy eu bank tests possession or experiencing an idea, so it cannot answer the source existential role. Prepare the explicit existential identity on lem_avoir with its own bank; all source words in il y a ___ remain intact.')
new('étonné','étonner','past participle masculine singular adjectival','astonished; surprised',['bored','calm','indifferent'],'Cette découverte le remplit d’une vive surprise : il est ___.',['étonné','ennuyé','calme','indifférent'],'Quel participe adjectival signifie frappé de surprise ?','sns_zola_etonner_surprise',note='Quelqu’un d’étonné is an astonished person hearing unexpected words, not someone shaken literally by thunder. The earlier étonnés/étonna plans target the published surprise sense; retain it, with a singular participial surface bank rather than a new adjective-only meaning.')
new('entendirent','entendre','verb past historic plural','heard; perceived by hearing',['saw','smelled','touched'],'Les paroles arrivèrent à leurs oreilles : ils les ___.',['entendirent','virent','sentirent','touchèrent'],'Quel verbe au passé simple pluriel indique une perception par l’ouïe ?','sns_cendrillon_entendre_percevoir_un_son_1d1dcaee8e',note='The humans hear the giant’s spoken address. The published auditory sense and VI entendre-understand proposal were compared; choose auditory perception for these words coming from an unknown location. All four predicates share the plural past construction and differ by sense modality.')
new('partaient','partir','verb imperfect plural origin','came from; originated',['arrived','stopped','disappeared'],'Les paroles étaient émises depuis un lieu : le verbe du récit pour cette origine est « ___ ».',['partaient','arrivaient','cessaient','disparaissaient'],'Quel verbe à l’imparfait pluriel signifie sortaient ou provenaient de cet endroit ?','new:lem_partir',note='Elles resumes the words, not female people leaving. D’où elles partaient asks where the sound originated. The published leave/set-out sense and à partir de starting-point construction were read; this emitted-sound origin is distinguished under the existing partir lemma. The source provides origin evidence; the text does not identify the speaker yet.')
new('aumônier','aumônier','noun masculine singular','chaplain',['sailor','surveyor','cook'],'Le prêtre chargé du service religieux à bord est l’___.',['aumônier','officier','arpenteur','ouvrier'],'Quel nom masculin désigne le prêtre chargé d’un service religieux auprès d’un groupe ?',note='The ship’s chaplain recites the prayers of exorcism. Aumônier/officier/arpenteur/ouvrier are masculine singular and all begin with a vowel, fitting unchanged l’. Only the clerical service role selects aumônier; elision cannot select it.')
new('récita','réciter','verb past historic singular','recited; said a text aloud',['wrote','erased','forgot'],'Il prononça à voix haute le texte des prières : il les ___.',['récita','écrivit','effaça','oublia'],'Quel verbe au passé simple signifie prononça un texte à voix haute ?',note='Récita names the aloud delivery of prayers, without inventing evidence that he read or memorized them. No existing or earlier réciter family exists. All four singular past predicates fit les as direct object; only recitation means saying the text aloud.')
new('prières','prière','noun feminine plural','prayers; words addressed to a deity',['letters','stories','songs'],'Les paroles religieuses adressées à Dieu sont des ___.',['prières','lettres','histoires','chansons'],'Quel nom féminin pluriel désigne des paroles adressées à une divinité ?',note='These are the prayers in the exorcism rite, rather than secular requests for a favor. Prières/lettres/histoires/chansons are feminine plural and fit des; religious address alone selects the target. Source association with exorcisms is retained without asserting that the rite works.')

new('exorcismes','exorcisme','noun masculine plural','exorcisms; rites intended to expel evil spirits',['journeys','calculations','judgments'],'Les rites religieux destinés à chasser un esprit mauvais sont des ___.',['exorcismes','voyages','calculs','jugements'],'Quel nom masculin pluriel désigne des rites destinés à chasser un esprit mauvais ?',note='The chaplain recites the prayers belonging to exorcisms in response to the unexplained voice. This is the narrator’s rite label, not evidence of supernatural efficacy. Exorcismes/voyages/calculs/jugements are masculine plural after des; the expulsion rite alone selects exorcismes.')
